From: jjude80 <18168364+jjude80@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:04:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(access): keep role-derived grants when a member's
 grants are replaced

Role-derived permissions are materialized as ordinary
principal_permission_grants rows, so any writer that replaces a principal's
grants must re-apply the role defaults or it silently strips the permissions
the membership role implies.

- setMemberPermissions and updateMemberAndPermissions now merge the role
  defaults back in instead of trusting every caller to pass the full set.
  Explicit grants still win on a key collision; agent principals are untouched
  because they have no role defaults.
- updateMember seeds the new role's defaults when membershipRole changes, so a
  promotion actually confers the role. Joining as an owner already did this;
  promotion did not.
- Agent principals keep exact set semantics (setMemberPermissions with
  ["tasks:assign"] still yields exactly that).

Verification: 28/28 in access-service.test.ts and
access-routes-permissions-upgrade.test.ts. With only the service changes
reverted, the 7 new/updated assertions fail. tsc --noEmit clean for the
server package.

